A||N||4||Monkeyman||I think my wife ate my cookies?||||9||
Z||000000||Monkeyman||01-26-2000||08:06 PM||||When I got home tonight I noticed that my tower had been moved.  I tried to log on to the Net, but had to provide my password.  Normally I have my password saved so I only have to click on IE and it does the rest for me.  (It took me about 5 tries before I came up with the right one!)  Once I got on to my home page (MSN) I noticed that some of the sections I keep on there weren't working.  (I finally got them back)  Also, I can always get my Hotmail names to come up just by typing the 1st letter but I couldn't do that either.  (Now that's working, too.)  Last, I logged onto the forum and noticed that every single thread had the open book icon next to it.  I went into the preferences and when I got back, all of the threads had the closed book icons.  I don't know much about computers, but is this just a loss of cookies?  If so, will everything be OK, now?  Can you lose your cookies (so to speak!) just by unplugging your computer without shutting it down?  I'm fairly sure that's what happened, but my wife's not home to ask her.  After that Happy99 thing, I've become pretty paranoid when something doesn't go right with this thing.  BTW-Nortons and McAfee say that I'm clean.||||reg||9
Z||000001||Cooter||01-26-2000||08:13 PM||||Monkeyman,<BR>My paranoid wife saw some files with my info in them so she deleted them. I now have no more bookmarked links or address book! I got pissed, but she was trying to help so I could not stay too mad. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Monkeyman||01-26-2000||08:22 PM||||If my wife was the one to mess things up (and I'm sure she was) I'm not mad at her.  I just want to make sure that everything's gonna be OK.  She doesn't mess with my computer at home as a rule and I don't mess with hers at work (EVER!).  My guess is that she was just trying to get to something behind the computer desk and bumped the power cord/tower or something like that.||||reg||1
Z||000003||william_thorniii||01-26-2000||08:31 PM||||FEAR NOT MONKEYMAN!<P>If all that happened was a loss of cookies, you are fine (afterall that happens most every weekend night at your local college...lol).  I just deleted mine to free up some space on my VERY FULL hard disk.  They will re-install the first time that you re-enter each of your sites.  The kicker is having to remember those passwords... Does this one support alpha/numeric or just alpha?  Was it max of 6 characters or min of 8?... Oh, (Phil stop reading now!) I need some of Monkey's meds!<P>William T. Thorn, III<P>A dog and a monkey in '04!<p>[This message has been edited by william_thorniii (edited 01-26-2000).]||||reg||10
Z||000004||fiero56||01-27-2000||12:13 AM||||Yeah, I'd say it was due to the power being cut off. Earlier today my computer started doing commands I didn't tell it to on the internet, so I got kina' mad and ripped the plug out of the wall. Well, I came back on and no more cookies. Took me a while to get everything typed back in. Remember, this was just after I learned I need another new clutch, so the computer was what finally set me over the edge. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||14
